# The Beast token can't block alone (CR 509.1b): blocking one of two attackers with it and nothing else is not a legal
# declaration of blockers, and with another creature of its controller blocking too it is. Bot2's two Memnites attack; the
# Beast alone is refused, and the Beast and Bot1's Memnite blocking one each is legal.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Toby, Beastie Befriender
Memnite
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite x2
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Toby, Beastie Befriender.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Memnite#1 > Bot1; Memnite#2 > Bot1)
! Bot1.Block(Beast Token > Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite#1)
Bot1.Block(Beast Token > Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite#1; Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite > Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite#2)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite; Memnite
Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite; Black Lotus
